		{
			dependencies: ["1DBBE96165C7987D"]
			description: [
				"When making circuits, you'll need either &9Liquid Tin&r, or &9Liquid Soldering Alloy&r&r&r. &2Soldering Alloy is made in the Mixer with 6 parts Tin Dust, 3 parts Lead Dust and 1 part Antimony Dust.&r You then process it in an &3Extractor &rfor the usual 144mB of fluid per unit."
				""
				"The &2Circuit Assembler&r will only consume half as much Soldering Alloy as it would have consumed Liquid Tin per craft (72mB vs 144mB), so it's very efficient to use this stuff."
				""
				"&2Antimony can be directly smelted from Stibnite Ore, allowing you to skip ore processing for this."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:soldering_alloy_bucket"
			id: "56924FC6B029BA0F"
