		{
			dependencies: ["6A914B240E1A7BCB"]
			description: [
				"&eSuperconductor wires won't kill you when touched. In fact, you have to use Wires for Superconductors, because they don't even have cables!"
				""
				"&bEnder IO&r and &bThermal&r alloys are a bit more expensive than the normal wires, but they come with the huge advantage of being &2superconductors&r. Lossy cables like &6Tin&r and &6Copper&r will bleed out energy for every block they travel, but &2superconductors&r do not."
				""
				"The &2cheap superconductors&r for each tier are:"
				""
				"LV - Conductive Iron"
				"MV - Energetic Alloy"
				"HV - Vibrant Alloy"
				"EV - End Steel"
				"IV - Lumium "
				"LuV - Signalum "
				"ZPM - Enderium "
				"UV - Cryolobus "
				"UHV - Sculk Superconductor"
				"UEV - Hyperdegenerate Darconite"
				"MAX - Monium"
				""
				"&2There are an additional set of superconductors, one for each tier, which are the GTm default superconductors. Their advantage is their higher amperage rating, reaching the hundreds of amps for higher tier 16x wires. They are also used in crafting Field Generators. They are:"
				""
				"LV - Manganese Phosphide"
				"MV - Magnesium Diboride"
				"HV - Mercury Barium Calcium Cuprate"
				"EV - Uranium Triplatinum"
				"IV - Samarium Iron Arsenic Oxide"
				"LuV - Indium Tin Barium Titanium Cuprate"
				"ZPM - Uranium Rhodium Dinaquadide"
				"UV - Enriched Naquadah Trinium Europium Duranide"
				"UHV - Ruthenium Trinium Americium Neutronate&r"
				"&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:energetic_alloy_octal_wire"
			id: "2861BA7C235C52A3"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{
				id: "7A50024966E38151"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&2Lossless Cables"
			x: 2.75d
			y: 17.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1BC6DDC2D50F9C46"]
			description: [
				"A machine's &amaximum recipe tier&r determines what recipes it can run. Under normal circumstances, the maximum recipe tier of a machine is equivalent to the machine tier for singleblock machines, or the tier of the energy hatch for multiblock machines."
				""
				"You may have noticed that you will need to run an &bMV&r recipe in your &3EBF&r to obtain &6Aluminium&r. Unfortunately, at this point you only have access to &7LV&r energy hatches."
				""
				"To get around this, you will need to raise the maximum recipe tier of your EBF higher than normal using the &eover-tiering&r mechanic."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Most multiblocks can have up to two &6Energy Hatches&r in their structure. The Energy Hatches you have access to are able to take in &a2 Amps&r of power each, as noted in their descriptions."
				""
				"Placing two &7LV&r &6Energy Hatches&r on your EBF lets you power the machine with total of four &7LV&r (32EU/t) amps, worth one &bMV&r (128EU/t) amp. This raises the maximum recipe tier of the EBF to &bMV&r, allowing it to run &bMV&r-tier recipes."
				""
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Raising the maximum recipe tier this way can result in &e&ooverclocking&r, which is a distinct mechanic not to be confused with over-tiering. You can read more about it \"},{\"underlined\":\"true\",\"text\":\"here\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"31AE366B15538079\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_voltage_coil"
			id: "02B78A0C4F3C4ECA"
			require_sequential_tasks: false
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "Not to be confused with overclocking"
			tasks: [{
				id: "480CE98BB705369B"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Recipe Tiers and Over-tiering"
			x: 2.75d
			y: 11.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"3BD20358F137E7C6"
				"5BE3E37772FAF6CB"
			]
			description: [
				"Once you have obtained your first pieces of &6Dark Steel&r, travel to the &bNether&r becomes available."
				""
				"The &eNether&r contains quite a few useful resources:"
				"- Some initial pieces of &6Sulfur&r"
				"- &6Glowstone&r and &6Soul Sand&r"
				"- &6Fluorine&r, &6Certus Quartz&r, &6Molybdenum&r, &6Antimony&r, and &6Gold&r-bearing ores"
				"- &2Nether Air&r, which can be distilled for useful gases"
				"- &eLava&r and &eNatural Gas&r from &2Fluid Rigs&r"
				""
				"In Normal Mode, &eNether&r travel is still strictly optional in the pack, although it is recommended."
			]
			hide_until_deps_visible: true
			id: "7A67E519745A8361"
			optional: true
			rewards: [{
				id: "5E252CA9C37789FE"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0E87A07E1757F58F"
				item: "telepastries:nether_cake"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 5.75d
			y: 2.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5C4E189A3E401566"]
			description: [
				"When a machine is operating at a higher recipe tier than what is required for running the current recipe, it will &aoverclock&r (&aOC&r) the recipe. Each overclock on a recipe will halve its duration but quadruple the rate of energy consumption. For example, a 30 EU/t recipe running in an &bMV&r machine will run at double speed but require 120EU/t."
				""
				"The only reason not to run recipes at higher speed is the additional power cost. If this is an issue, you might want to build more lower tier machines in place of overclocking."
				""
				"Additionally, &8ULV&r recipes will not overclock to &7LV&r. A ≤8 EU/t recipe won't overclock at all in an &7LV&r machine, and will only overclock once in an &bMV&r machine, etc."
				""
				"Overclocks can be visualized with the help of &bEMI&r by interacting with the voltage tier indicator in the bottom right of machine recipes."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:clock"
			id: "31AE366B15538079"
			subtitle: "Not to be confused with over-tiering"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2C6BF4196CE9468F"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Overclocking"
			x: -5.5d
			y: 7.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1BC6DDC2D50F9C46"]
			description: [
				"Your shiny new &3Electric Blast Furnace&r can be used to process ores like regular &3Furnaces&r."
				""
				"Unlike Furnaces, However, your &3Electric Blast Furnace&r holds a more specialized role: it is highly efficient at maximizing the resources you get out of sulfuric ores like &6Galena&r, &6Chalcopyrite&r, and &6Cobaltite&r."
				""
				"This refinement produces &9Sulfur Dioxide&r as a byproduct, which is useful for the production of &9Sulfuric Acid&r."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:hot_mercury_barium_calcium_cuprate_ingot"
			id: "14C50EFF4EB257E3"
			tasks: [{
				id: "01FA8F1646AC977B"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Sulfuric Ore Pyrometallurgy"
			x: 4.25d
			y: 14.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2EF8EE4CC34F8D09"]
			description: [
				"&6Batteries&r are &bGregTech &rpower storage for &aEU&r energy."
				""
				"&2Lithium Batteries&r have the highest capacity, but &6Sodium&r and &6Cadmium Batteries&r are also perfectly useful in &7LV&r. Charged batteries of all three types can be found in &bLost Cities&r loot chests, with extra chances on the sixth floor and above."
				""
				"For a renewable source of &6Sodium&r and &6Lithium Dust&r, electrolyze &6Clay Dust&r in an &7LV&r &3Electrolyzer&r. You can also buy Lithium Ore with &9Monicoins&r."
			]
